1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,170
一亿度的火，
A fire at one hundred million degrees

2
00:00:01,170 --> 00:00:03,330
就关在合肥的一个“炉子”里。
is locked inside a 'furnace' in Hefei.

3
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:03,940
一亿度，
A hundred million degrees.

4
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:05,600
是太阳核心的六七倍。
Six or seven times the core of the Sun.

5
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,790
这几天，抖音博主钻进“人造太阳”拍视频，
This week, Douyin creators filmed inside China's 'artificial sun',

6
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:10,350
上了科学热榜第一。
topping the science trending list.

7
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:12,020
B站的科学晚会上，
At Bilibili's science night,

8
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:13,820
人造太阳也是主角。
the artificial sun was a star too.

9
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:14,980
它叫东方超环，
It's called EAST.

10
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:18,100
2025年1月，跑出了“亿度千秒”。
In January 2025 it held its plasma for over a thousand seconds.

11
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:19,570
一千零六十六秒，
One thousand sixty-six seconds,

12
00:00:19,570 --> 00:00:20,970
将近十八分钟。
almost eighteen minutes.

13
00:00:20,970 --> 00:00:22,340
今天的烧脑问题：
Today's brain teaser:

14
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:25,560
一亿度，什么墙不化？凭啥烧不穿炉子？
at a hundred million degrees, every wall melts. Why doesn't the furnace burn through?

15
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:26,770
先认识主角：
Meet our hero:

16
00:00:26,770 --> 00:00:29,130
一亿度的小火球，亿亿。
a tiny hundred-million-degree fireball, Yiyi.

17
00:00:29,130 --> 00:00:31,000
这么热，原子都被扯散了，
At that heat, atoms get torn apart:

18
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,830
电子和原子核各跑各的。
electrons and nuclei run separately.

19
00:00:32,830 --> 00:00:34,380
这团带电的“汤”，
This charged soup

20
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:35,530
叫等离子体。
is called plasma.

21
00:00:35,530 --> 00:00:36,240
反转一：
Twist one:

22
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:38,310
炉子的墙，根本不碰火。
the wall never touches the fire.

23
00:00:38,310 --> 00:00:40,040
带电的粒子一进磁场，
Charged particles in a magnetic field

24
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:42,070
就只能绕着磁力线打转。
can only spiral around the field lines.

25
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:44,290
磁力线就像过山车的轨道，
Field lines are like roller-coaster tracks.

26
00:00:44,290 --> 00:00:47,010
车只能顺着轨道跑，跳不出去。
The cars follow the track and can't jump off.

27
00:00:47,010 --> 00:00:48,960
把轨道首尾接成一个圈，
Join the track into a loop

28
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:51,200
就是个甜甜圈形的磁笼子。
and you get a doughnut-shaped magnetic cage.

29
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:52,000
这种笼子，
This cage

30
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,090
叫托卡马克。
is called a tokamak.

31
00:00:53,090 --> 00:00:54,650
火球在中间飘着，
The fireball floats in the middle,

32
00:00:54,650 --> 00:00:55,940
离墙远远的。
far from the wall.

33
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:58,340
太阳靠自己巨大的引力压住火，
The Sun holds its fire with huge gravity.

34
00:00:58,340 --> 00:00:59,830
我们只能靠磁场。
We only have magnets.

35
00:00:59,830 --> 00:01:02,300
也正因为没有太阳那么大的压力，
And without the Sun's crushing pressure,

36
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:04,230
温度只好比太阳高得多。
we have to go much hotter than the Sun.

37
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:04,900
反转二：
Twist two:

38
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:06,890
一亿度，其实没多少热。
a hundred million degrees isn't much heat.

39
00:01:06,890 --> 00:01:08,610
温度是粒子跑得多快，
Temperature is how fast particles move.

40
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:10,610
热量还要看粒子有多少。
Heat also depends on how many there are.

41
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:12,840
估算一下：炉子里的等离子体，
A rough estimate: the plasma is

42
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:14,540
比空气还稀几十万倍。
a few hundred thousand times thinner than air.

43
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:16,270
就像过年的仙女棒，
Like a sparkler:

44
00:01:16,270 --> 00:01:19,070
火花上千度，落在手上却不烫。
sparks over a thousand degrees, yet they don't burn your hand.

45
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:20,530
火花太小、太少，
The sparks are too small and too few.

46
00:01:20,530 --> 00:01:22,670
热量还没传过来就没了。
Their heat is gone before it reaches you.

47
00:01:22,670 --> 00:01:24,550
所以万一磁笼子失灵，
So if the cage ever fails,

48
00:01:24,550 --> 00:01:26,940
火球一碰墙，自己先凉了。
the fireball hits the wall and cools itself first.

49
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:29,060
人造太阳不会像炸弹那样炸，
An artificial sun can't explode like a bomb.

50
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:30,490
它只会“熄火”。
It just goes out.

51
00:01:30,490 --> 00:01:32,060
当然墙也会受点伤，
The wall does get hurt a little,

52
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:34,440
所以墙要用耐高温的钨来做。
so it's armored with tough tungsten.

53
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:36,130
反转三，最反直觉：
Twist three, the weirdest:

54
00:01:36,130 --> 00:01:38,500
最热的旁边，就是最冷的。
right next to the hottest thing is the coldest.

55
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:40,110
磁笼子靠超导线圈，
The cage uses superconducting coils

56
00:01:40,110 --> 00:01:42,380
要冷到零下二百六十九度。
chilled to minus two hundred sixty-nine degrees.

57
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:45,140
一边一亿度，一边接近绝对零度，
A hundred million degrees on one side, almost absolute zero on the other,

58
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:47,660
中间就隔一层真空和几层墙。
with just a vacuum and a few layers between.

59
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:48,950
就像热水瓶，
It's like a thermos:

60
00:01:48,950 --> 00:01:52,080
中间抽成真空，热就传不过去。
the vacuum in between stops the heat.

61
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:53,600
费这么大劲图啥？
Why go to all this trouble?

62
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,230
燃料就在海水里。
The fuel is in seawater.

63
00:01:55,230 --> 00:01:58,440
B站晚会上说：一瓶海水里的聚变能，
At Bilibili's science night they said: the fusion energy in one bottle of seawater

64
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:00,250
够开车跑一千公里。
could drive a car a thousand kilometers.

65
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:02,980
友情提示：现在还发不出能卖的电，
Fine print: it can't sell electricity yet.

66
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:04,800
我们推测还要很多年。
Our guess: that's still many years away.

67
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:07,270
比稀薄几十万倍，是我们的估算；
Thinner by hundreds of thousands is our estimate.

68
00:02:07,270 --> 00:02:09,540
一千公里，是晚会上的说法。
The thousand kilometers is what the show said.

69
00:02:09,540 --> 00:02:11,920
所以，一亿度凭啥烧不穿炉子？
So why doesn't a hundred million degrees burn through?

70
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:14,590
因为火碰不到墙，而且它太稀了。
The fire never touches the wall, and it's very thin.

71
00:02:14,590 --> 00:02:15,940
人造太阳的秘密，
The secret of the artificial sun

72
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:19,490
不是更结实的炉子，是一个看不见的笼子。
is not a stronger furnace, but an invisible cage.

